  "summary": "Traditional yarn paintings created by the Wixarika (Huichol) people using beeswax and colored yarn.",
  "description": "Features intricate symbolic designs depicting spiritual visions and cultural narratives, created by pressing colored yarn onto boards coated with beeswax and pine resin. Developed as an art form in the early 20th century as a means of cultural preservation and economic survival, adapting traditional ceremonial practices into a portable art form.",
